			<div class="content" id="post-content-1719599">
									

<p>The picture of the doll feels off to me in a way that I can not pin down.<br />
Is that a life-size doll, a real person made-up to look doll-like, or what?<br />
I see a few stray hairs off the top of her head, and the focus seems consistent, so I'm thinking it's not photoshoppery. But it's way too life-like for the macro dolls I've seen, and one hell of an accomlishment if it's a live lady cosplaying Barbie.</p>
<p>Story itself is a bit cliche, but solidly executed and avoids the biggest pitfalls. No rage state or flesh-doll gore, for example. +1</p>
<p>Edit: Just a note that I was talking about a former picture. The current one is just a close up of a standard fashion doll.<br />
Also, I guess that picture was a big part of what I liked. Or maybe my tastes have changed over the past six years. Re-reading today I just find it kind of boring. Swap to -1.</p>

							</div>

								
